{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The execution date is left as \"July ¥, 2005\", so the \"Effective Date\" — the anchor for the Employment Term, the commission period and the severance end-date — is not legible on the face of the instrument. That is a mechanical defect that a court could be asked to fix by extrinsic evidence.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
   {"issue": "The preamble makes both Ajuba and Ajuba India jointly the \"Company\", yet Section 2.1 has only Ajuba India employ him and Sections 2.2/8.4 make only Ajuba India the payor. Which entity owes the obligations is arguable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": "This states that \"the Company\" (both entities) employs the Employee, while Section 2.1 states that Ajuba India employs him as President of Ajuba India. The identity of the employer is left inconsistent.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
   {"issue": "\"Board\" is Ajuba's board, but Section 2.1 has the Employee report \"directly to the Board (or selected designee of the Board of Directors of the Parent)\" and Schedule 2.1 says he reports to the Chairman. The reporting line is not uniform.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition ends with the open catch-alls \"such other entities serviced by the Company\" and \"other related services\" after a long enumerated list, so the outer boundary of \"Business\" — the term that fixes the reach of the Article V noncompete — is uncertain. That is a classic ejusdem generis / general-vs-specific problem.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.45},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.04},
   {"issue": "\"Code\" is defined but never used anywhere in the operative text, which is surplusage rather than a conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Known to the Employee as a consequence of or through the Employee's employment\" makes ownership turn on how knowledge was acquired, a boundary that cannot be applied to ideas the Employee brought with him or learned independently. The phrase is vague on its face.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
   {"issue": "Section 4.1 assigns technology \"conceived, developed or acquired during the Employment Term\", a different trigger from this definition's \"known to the Employee as a consequence of\" his employment. The two capture different bodies of material.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"All information, in whatever form, regarding Parent, the Company their Business and their clients\" is unbounded, and the ten enumerated categories are introduced by \"without limitation\", leaving the catch-all's reach against the specifics unsettled. There is also no carve-out in the definition itself for public or independently known information.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition is internally tangled: limb (a) already covers everything provided to healthcare-industry entities, which appears to swallow the quantitative test in limb (b), and limb (b)(ii)'s \"more than the sum of (A) ... and (B)\" formula is hard to apply. The scope of \"Core Business\" is genuinely uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The lookback periods run from \"the date of termination of this Agreement\", but it is the Employee's employment, not the Agreement, that terminates, and \"actively sought\" and \"material contact\" are undefined. The class of protected Customers is therefore imprecise.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Disputes over EBITDA are committed to \"the independent accountants regularly employed by Ajuba\", a one-sided mechanism whose finality (binding? appealable?) is not stated. A court could be asked whether that determination forecloses a bonus claim.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
   {"issue": "This runs the Term to \"the third anniversary of this Agreement\" while Section 8.1 runs it to \"the third anniversary of the Effective Date\"; with an illegible execution date those need not coincide. The mismatch also drives the Restricted Period in Section 1.14.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.05},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.04},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.05},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Three years after the end of the Employment Term\" is ambiguous where employment ends early: the end may be the actual termination date or the scheduled third anniversary under Section 1.9. That difference can move the expiry of the Article V covenants by years.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The section commands \"full professional and business-related time, skills and best efforts\" and duties \"customarily performed by a President\", then permits unspecified passive investments and outside board seats, leaving the line between permitted and forbidden activity indistinct. \"Customarily performed by a President\" has no fixed content.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
   {"issue": "Schedule 2.1 is stated to control over the Bylaws and yet is \"deemed to have been amended\" by any consolidation or outsourcing described in Section 8.4(a), so the duties that fix a Good Reason \"material diminution\" can be unilaterally rewritten. The interaction with Section 8.4(a) is not coherent.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The salary step-up is \"retroactive to the first business day of the year following the Fiscal Year in which such EBITDA was achieved\", which is retroactive to a future date and does not say whether the trigger applies once or in any year. The escalation date is genuinely unclear.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
   {"issue": "The Allowance is paid \"in lieu of receiving health, dental and other benefits afforded to Ajuba US employees\", while Section 2.2(c) entitles the Employee to participate in all benefit plans made available to senior executives. The two benefit entitlements are hard to reconcile.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Employee is only \"eligible to receive\" the Bonus and the table gives discrete EBITDA points with no rule for results between or above the tiers or for prorating. Whether a Bonus is earned at all, and in what amount, is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
   {"issue": "The final sentence conditions the FY2007 Bonus on service \"through the entire Employment Term\" unless terminated under Sections 8.3 or 8.4, while Sections 8.2 and 8.5 disclaim liability for any bonus \"for either the prior or current year\". The carve-outs and disclaimers do not line up.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
